# Before you deploy the Counter change

Your existing issues already have IDs generated from `countDocuments()`. If the
counter starts at 0, the next report regenerates `SB-2026-00001` and hits the
unique index.

Seed the counter once, from the Mongo shell or a one-off script:

```js
// backend/seed/seedCounter.js
const mongoose = require('mongoose');
const Issue    = require('../models/Issue');
const Counter  = require('../models/Counter');

(async () => {
  await mongoose.connect(process.env.MONGO_URI);
  const year = new Date().getFullYear();

  const ids = await Issue.find({ grievanceId: new RegExp(`^SB-${year}-`) })
                         .select('grievanceId').lean();

  const max = ids.reduce((m, d) => {
    const n = parseInt(d.grievanceId.split('-')[2], 10);
    return Number.isNaN(n) ? m : Math.max(m, n);
  }, 0);

  await Counter.findByIdAndUpdate(
    `issue-${year}`,
    { seq: max },
    { upsert: true }
  );

  console.log(`Counter issue-${year} seeded to ${max}`);
  process.exit(0);
})();
```

Run once: `node seed/seedCounter.js`

Repeat for any earlier year that has data (`SB-2024-*`, `SB-2025-*`) only if you
might still create issues dated to those years. Normally you won't.